The code snippet you provided is a part of PEX testing source code for the Microsoft's Pex library. The Pex library automates the practice of white-box fuzz testing (which means it tries randomly generated inputs to your code and checks assertions on outputs). So, Assert statements are written to validate that certain conditions hold true at the end of every execution path of your methods.

Pex testing uses assertions for verification of important properties, they also check pre/post-conditions, invariant conditions, and state changes. This is why your comments "@@@ last position of x in new array list is greater than or equal to that in old array" maps to `Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX >= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);`.

For more information, refer to the official Pex documentation: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/test/extending-pex-testing-csharp-in-visual-studio?view=vs-2022--------------------
